 "description": "A new SRC machine, DIGISLICER: the SLICE machine with a slice editor. Its SRC page is SLICE's; press SRC again for the editor, where you slice the sample where you want (add at a cursor, split, delete, move, auto-slice on transients, equal grids), watch it play and play slices from the trig keys. A sample's own slices play on every DIGISLICER track and are kept per sample on the +Drive (/cfw/slices.a, .b). GRID also gets AUTO (slices on the transients) and PLAY gets PIPO (ping-pong loops). The stock SLICE machine is left as it is.",
